## \uc0\u55358 \u56810  \u37197 \u22871 \u27979 \u35797 \u31574 \u30053 \u65288 Vitest\u65289 \
\
\uc0\u27599 \u20010 \u20989 \u25968 \u37197  3-5 \u20010 \u27979 \u35797 \u29992 \u20363 \u65292 \u37325 \u28857 \u35206 \u30422 \u65306 \
1. **Happy Path**\uc0\u65306 \u27491 \u24120 \u36755 \u20837 \
2. **Edge Case**\uc0\u65306 `null`\u12289 `undefined`\u12289 \u31354 \u25968 \u32452 \u12289 \u24490 \u29615 \u24341 \u29992 \
3. **Type Safety**\uc0\u65306 TS \u32534 \u35793 \u26399 \u26816 \u26597 \u65288 \u21487 \u29992  `expectTypeOf` \u25110 \u27880 \u37322 \u35828 \u26126 \u65289 \
\
```typescript\
// tests/array/chunk.test.ts\
import \{ describe, it, expect \} from 'vitest';\
import \{ chunk \} from '../../src/array/chunk';\
\
describe('chunk', () => \{\
  it('should split array into chunks', () => \{\
    expect(chunk([1, 2, 3, 4], 2)).toEqual([[1, 2], [3, 4]]);\
  \});\
\
  it('should return empty array for null/undefined', () => \{\
    expect(chunk(null)).toEqual([]);\
    expect(chunk(undefined)).toEqual([]);\
  \});\
\
  it('should handle last chunk smaller than size', () => \{\
    expect(chunk([1, 2, 3], 2)).toEqual([[1, 2], [3]]);\
  \});\
\});\
```\
